  "Question": "The supplement of an angle is 3 times its complement. How many degrees is the angle?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "45",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Let the angle measure \\(x^\\circ\\). Then \\(180-x=3(90-x)\\), which gives \\(x=45\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Use the 90° difference\n\nThe supplement and complement are found by subtracting the same angle from \\(180^\\circ\\) and \\(90^\\circ\\), so their difference is \\(180^\\circ-90^\\circ=90^\\circ\\). The supplement is three copies of the complement, so this difference is two copies of the complement. Therefore the complement measures \\(90^\\circ\\div2=45^\\circ\\), and the angle measures \\(90^\\circ-45^\\circ=45^\\circ\\).",
